course: dictionary
lesson: 8045
title: Feeling sorry: regret
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To regret something means to feel sorry or sad about something you did, or did not do, and to wish it had been different. Regret can be a verb, as in «I regret it», or a noun, as in «a feeling of regret».
explain: «Some feuds are never mended, and people often regret it for the rest of their lives.» Here regret means they keep feeling sorry about the quarrel for a long time. The clue is the words «never mended», which tell you the people wish things had gone differently.
explain: «Regret is the feeling of wishing you had not done something; it can help you choose better next time.» This sentence shows the noun. The words after the semicolon explain it: wishing you had not done something. Then you can use that feeling to make a better choice.
fact: To regret something means to feel sorry about something you did or did not do, and wish it had been different.
fact: «Regret» can be a verb (regret, regrets, regretted, regretting) or a noun (regret, regrets).
fact: Useful phrases include «to my regret», «no regrets» and «regret doing».
fact: In polite, formal writing, «We regret to inform you» means «We are sorry to say».
fact: «Regret» is a feeling that can teach you, so think about what you would do differently next time.
exercise: «I regret breaking my sister's toy, and I wish I could take it back.» What does regret mean here? | Laugh about something you did | *Feel sorry about something you did | Feel very proud of something you did | Forget about something you did
exercise: «Ella felt a deep regret after she lied to her friend.» What does regret mean in this sentence? | To run away quickly | A loud shout of joy | A kind of food | *The sad, sorry feeling
exercise: «Some feuds are never mended, and people often regret it for the rest of their lives.» What does regret it mean? | Mend it at once | Forget it straight away | *Wish they had not done it and feel sorry | Are very happy about it
test: In a letter, the school writes: «We regret to inform you that the trip is cancelled.» What does regret mean here? | *We are sorry to say | We are going to say nothing | We are angry about the weather | We are very excited to say
test: Choose the correct past form: «Yesterday Sam ___ forgetting his homework.» | regret | *regretted | regretting | regrets
exam: «I have no regrets about moving here,» said Maya. What does no regrets mean? | She wants to move again tomorrow | She is very sad about moving | *She does not feel sorry about moving | She has lost her home
